Article 13 Where a foreign country submits a request for criminal judicial assistance to the People's Republic of China, it shall submit the request in accordance with the provisions of the criminal judicial assistance treaty. Where there is no treaty or the treaty has no provisions, the request shall specify the following matters and attach relevant materials:
(1) the name of the requesting authority;
(2) the nature of the case, basic information on the persons involved, and the facts of the crime;
(3) the legal provisions applicable to this case;
(4) the matters and purpose of the request;
(5) the relevance between the requested matters and the case;
(6) the time limit within which the request is expected to be executed;
(7) other necessary information or additional requirements.
In the absence of a criminal judicial assistance treaty, the requesting country shall make a commitment of reciprocity.
The request and attached materials shall be accompanied by a translation in Chinese.

Article 14 Where a foreign country submits a request for criminal judicial assistance to the People's Republic of China, assistance may be refused under any of the following circumstances:
(1) the conduct for which the request is made does not constitute a crime according to the laws of the People's Republic of China;
(2) at the time of receiving the request, an investigation, inquiry, prosecution, or adjudication is ongoing within the territory of the People's Republic of China with respect to the crime for which the request is made, a final judgment has been rendered, the criminal proceedings have been terminated, or the statute of limitations for prosecution of the crime has expired;
(3) the crime for which the request is made is a political crime;
(4) the crime for which the request is made is a purely military crime;
(5) the purpose of the request is to conduct investigation, inquiry, prosecution, adjudication, or execution of a sentence on grounds of race, ethnicity, religion, nationality, gender, political opinion, or identity, or the party may be subjected to unfair treatment due to the above reasons;
(6) there is a lack of substantial connection between the requested matters and the case for which assistance is requested;
(7) other circumstances where refusal is permissible.

Article 16 After receiving the request for criminal judicial assistance and the attached materials transmitted by the foreign liaison authority, the competent authority shall review them and shall handle them separately as follows:
(1) where it finds that assistance may be executed in accordance with the provisions of this Law and the criminal judicial assistance treaty, it shall make a decision and arrange for the relevant case-handling authority to execute it;
(2) where it finds that assistance shall be refused in whole or in part in accordance with the provisions of Articles 4 and 14 of this Law or the criminal judicial assistance treaty, it shall return the request and attached materials to the foreign liaison authority and provide reasons;
(3) where there are confidentiality requirements or other additional conditions for executing the request, it shall raise them through the foreign liaison authority to the foreign country, and after the foreign country accepts the conditions and provides a written guarantee, decide to execute the request with conditions;
(4) where supplementary materials are needed, it shall notify the foreign liaison authority in writing to request the requesting country to provide them within a reasonable period.
Where executing the request may impede an ongoing investigation, inquiry, prosecution, adjudication, or execution by a relevant authority of the People's Republic of China, the competent authority may decide to postpone assistance and shall notify the foreign liaison authority in writing of the decision and reasons for postponement.
Where a foreign country has confidentiality requirements or special procedural requirements for executing its request, the competent authority may arrange execution in accordance with those requirements, provided that it does not violate the basic principles of the laws of the People's Republic of China.

Article 25 Where a case-handling authority needs the assistance of a foreign country in the following matters for investigation and evidence collection, it shall prepare a request for criminal judicial assistance with relevant materials attached, and after the request is reviewed and approved by the competent authority to which it belongs, the foreign liaison authority shall promptly submit the request to the foreign country:
(1) locating or identifying relevant persons;
(2) inquiring into or verifying information on property and financial accounts involved in the case;
(3) obtaining and providing testimony or statements of relevant persons;
(4) obtaining and providing relevant documents, records, electronic data, and objects;
(5) obtaining and providing expert opinions;
(6) inspecting or examining places, objects, persons, or bodies;
(7) searching persons, objects, residences, and other relevant places;
(8) other matters.
When requesting a foreign country to assist in investigation and evidence collection, the case-handling authority may at the same time request to dispatch personnel to be present during the execution of the request.

Article 26 Where investigation and evidence collection is requested from a foreign country, the request and attached materials shall, as necessary, specify the following matters:
(1) the name, gender, address, identity information, contact details, and other information helpful in identifying the person to be investigated;
(2) the questions to be asked to the person to be investigated;
(3) the name, gender, address, identity information, contact details, appearance and behavioral characteristics, and other information helpful in locating or identifying the person to be located or identified;
(4) specific information on the ownership, location, characteristics, form, and quantity of the property involved in the case to be inquired into or verified, and relevant information on financial accounts to be inquired into or verified;
(5) specific information on the holder, location, characteristics, form, and quantity of the relevant documents, records, electronic data, and objects to be obtained;
(6) specific information on the object to be evaluated;
(7) specific information on the places, objects, etc., to be inspected or examined;
(8) specific information on the object to be searched;
(9) other materials helpful in executing the request.

Article 32 Where a request is made to a foreign State to arrange for a witness or expert evaluator to testify or assist in an investigation, the Letter of Request and the attached materials shall, as necessary, contain the following:
(1) The name, gender, address, identity information, contact information of the witness or expert evaluator, and other information helpful for confirming the identity of the witness or expert evaluator;
(2) The purpose, necessity, time and place of the testimony or assistance in the investigation;
(3) The rights and obligations of the witness or expert evaluator;
(4) Measures for the protection of the witness or expert evaluator;
(5) Subsidies for the witness or expert evaluator;
(6) Other materials helpful for executing the request.

Article 40 Where a request is made to a foreign State for sealing, seizing, or freezing property involved in a case, the Letter of Request and the attached materials shall, as necessary, contain the following:
(1) The proof of ownership, name, characteristics, form, and quantity of the property involved in a case to be sealed, seized, or frozen;
(2) The location of the property involved in a case to be sealed, seized, or frozen. If funds or other financial assets are deposited with a financial institution, the name, address, and account information of the financial institution shall be stated;
(3) Copies of the relevant legal documents;
(4) Legal provisions concerning sealing, seizure, and freezing as well as the protection of the rights of interested parties;
(5) Other materials helpful for executing the request.

Article 43 If, after examination, the competent authority finds that the following conditions are met, it may agree to seal, seize, or freeze the property involved in the case and arrange for the relevant case-handling authority to execute the request:
(1) The sealing, seizure, or freezing meets the conditions prescribed by the laws of the People's Republic of China;
(2) The sealing, seizure, or freezing of the property involved in the case is related to the investigation, inquiry, prosecution, and adjudication activities of a criminal case pending in the requesting State;
(3) The property involved in the case may be sealed, seized, or frozen;
(4) The execution of the request does not affect the lawful rights and interests of interested parties;
(5) The execution of the request does not affect the ongoing investigation, inquiry, prosecution, adjudication, and enforcement activities of the relevant authorities of the People's Republic of China.
The case-handling authority shall promptly notify the foreign liaison authority through the competent authority, and the foreign liaison authority shall inform the requesting State of the results of the sealing, seizure, or freezing. When necessary, the case-handling authority may, according to law, take measures to dispose of the sealed, seized, or frozen property involved in the case.

Article 48 Where a request is made to a foreign State for the confiscation or return of illegal gains and other property involved in a case, the Letter of Request and the attached materials shall, as necessary, contain the following:
(1) The name, characteristics, form, and quantity of the illegal gains and other property involved in a case to be confiscated or returned;
(2) The location of the illegal gains and other property involved in a case to be confiscated or returned. If funds or other financial assets are deposited with a financial institution, the name, address, and account information of the financial institution shall be stated;
(3) The reasons for confiscation or return and relevant proof of ownership;
(4) Copies of the relevant legal documents;
(5) Legal provisions concerning confiscation, return, and the protection of the rights of interested parties;
(6) Other materials helpful for executing the request.

Article 51 Where the competent authority, upon review, considers that the following conditions are met, it may agree to assist in confiscation of illegal gains and other property involved in a case and arrange for the relevant case-handling authority to execute:
(1) The confiscation of illegal gains and other property involved in a case satisfies the conditions provided for by the laws of the People's Republic of China;
(2) The foreign country has fully protected the relevant rights of interested parties;
(3) There is property available for execution within the People's Republic of China;
(4) The request letter and attached materials describe in detail the ownership, name, characteristics, shape, quantity and other information of the property targeted by the request;
(5) The confiscation cannot be executed or cannot be fully executed in the requesting country;
(6) Other conditions that the competent authority deems necessary to be satisfied.

Article 52 Where a foreign country requests assistance in confiscation of illegal gains and other property involved in a case, assistance may be refused and reasons shall be given if any of the following circumstances exists:
(1) The judicial authority of the People's Republic of China or a third country has rendered a legally effective judgment on the property targeted by the request and the judgment has been executed or is being executed;
(2) The property targeted by the request does not exist, has been damaged, lost, sold, or has been transferred and thus cannot be executed, unless the request is for confiscation of the proceeds from sale or the transferred property;
(3) The person targeted by the request has debts not yet satisfied or lawsuits not yet concluded within the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(4) Other circumstances under which refusal is permissible.

Article 56 The transfer of a sentenced person to a foreign country shall meet the following conditions:
(1) The sentenced person is a national of that country;
(2) The act for which the sentenced person was sentenced to a penalty also constitutes a crime under the law of that country;
(3) The judgment imposing the penalty on the sentenced person has taken legal effect;
(4) The sentenced person gives written consent to the transfer, or, if necessary due to the sentenced person's age, physical or mental condition, the sentenced person's agent gives written consent to the transfer;
(5) Both the People's Republic of China and that country consent to the transfer.
The transfer may be refused under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The sentenced person is sentenced to death with a two-year reprieve or life imprisonment, unless the sentence has been commuted to fixed-term imprisonment at the time of the request for transfer;
(2) At the time of the request for transfer, the remaining term of the sentenced person's sentence is less than one year;
(3) The sentenced person has pending lawsuits within the territory of the People's Republic of China;
(4) Other circumstances where transfer is not appropriate.

Article 57 Where a request is made to transfer a sentenced person to a foreign country, the request letter and attached materials shall, as necessary, specify the following matters:
(1) The name of the requesting authority;
(2) The name, sex, nationality, identity information and other data of the sentenced person sought to be transferred;
(3) The place where the sentenced person is serving the sentence;
(4) The basis and reasons for the request for transfer;
(5) The written statement of consent to the transfer by the sentenced person or his/her agent;
(6) Other matters.

Article 64 The People's Procuratorate shall prepare an application for conversion of penalty and attach relevant materials, and submit it to the Intermediate People's Court at the location of the penal enforcement authority for a ruling on conversion of penalty.
The People's Court shall, based on the facts determined in the judgment of the foreign court and in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Law, render a ruling on conversion of penalty. Where the nature and duration of the penalty imposed by the foreign court are in conformity with the provisions of the laws of the People's Republic of China, the conversion shall be carried out in accordance with the nature and duration of the penalty imposed; where the nature and duration of the penalty imposed by the foreign court are not in conformity with the provisions of the laws of the People's Republic of China, the type and term of the penalty shall be determined in accordance with the following principles:
(1) The converted penalty shall, to the extent possible, be consistent with the penalty imposed by the foreign court;
(2) The converted penalty shall not be heavier in nature or term than the penalty imposed by the foreign court, nor shall it exceed the maximum penalty prescribed by the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China for the same type of crime;
(3) A penalty of deprivation of liberty shall not be converted into a property penalty;
(4) The converted penalty shall not be bound by the minimum penalty prescribed by the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China for the same type of crime.
Where the sentenced person is detained before being returned to China to serve the sentence, each day of pre-sentence custody shall be counted as one day of the converted sentence.
The ruling on conversion of penalty rendered by the People's Court is a final ruling.
